    {
      "short": "Right-size DR",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "Buy what your SLA requires",
      "body": [
        "Multi-region <span class=\"term\">active-active</span> doubles infrastructure cost and forces you to answer 'which region owns this write?' — data consistency across regions is genuinely hard.",
        "Overprovisioning for failure means most days you're paying for capacity you don't use. That's not waste — that's insurance."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Region B: full K8s + DynamoDB stack",
        "+ Cross-region data sync",
        "~ CDN failover now routes around a dead region"
      ],
